 },
 "HEADLINE": {
  "step_1_rho_equal_bins": "the fixed-term AXIS still rotates on rho-EQUAL bins, so the rotation is NOT an artefact of equal-count binning: span 16.5 deg, chi2 74.6 on 4 dof (rho-equal) against 17.4 deg, chi2 95.1 (equal-count), both with the anomalous frame excluded.",
  "step_2_constancy": "NO f makes the residual a constant 2-vector. chi2/dof = 19.3 on 7 dof (rho-equal) and 30.3 (equal-count). The best-fit f runs 5.7-7.6, i.e. 6-8x the predicted trail, which is what a MISSPECIFIED model returns rather than a trail measurement.",
  "PRE_REGISTERED_OUTCOME_THAT_FIRED": "'No f makes the residual constant' -> there is no field-constant optical component, and corner-fix-landscape's rl -loadpsf= route dies. CONDITIONAL on excluding DSC_6239 (see below).",
  "THE_ERROR_MODEL_IS_THE_REAL_FINDING_AND_IT_CORRECTS_ME": {
   "what": "the per-bin fixed term's uncertainty was taken from a STAR-LEVEL bootstrap inside one pooled population. That captures shot noise only.",
   "measured": "against the 5 raws as INDEPENDENT realisations, the frame-to-frame scatter is 4.1-9.2x the bootstrap SE, median 5.76x.",
   "consequence": "chi2/dof 35.6 with bootstrap errors becomes ~1.1 with frame-based errors. The bootstrap turns 'cannot reject' into a spurious rejection.",
   "what_it_retracts": "the recorded '10 to 20 sigma' on the fixed term's 22 deg rotation used those bootstrap SEs (1.07-1.39 deg). With frame-based errors the SEs are 0.83-2.58 deg on four frames, or 4.3-12.6 deg on five. The ROTATION SURVIVES but the quoted significance did not, and the finding's dependence on one frame's exclusion was never stated.",
   "rule": "a per-bin property estimated from N frames has N independent realisations; resampling stars inside a pooled population is not an error bar for it."
  },
  "THE_RESULT_HINGES_ON_ONE_FRAME_AND_THAT_MUST_TRAVEL_WITH_IT": {
   "with_all_5_frames": "axis constancy chi2 = 3.0/4 (rho-equal) \u2014 does NOT reject. Full fit chi2/dof = 1.81 \u2014 does NOT reject. Nothing is concluded.",
   "dropping_DSC_6239": "chi2 = 74.6/4 and 19.3/7 \u2014 both reject decisively.",
   "why_the_exclusion_is_principled_and_pre-documented": "DSC_6239 is the first-frame-of-night anomaly already on the record in two other quantities (theta0 departs 19.75 deg while the drift bearing departs 0.150 deg; and coherent_trail's own gate 1B reads it at 0.4615 against 0.757-0.815 for the other four). Its per-bin axes here are -35.9/-44.5/-40.2/-30.4/-3.5 against the other four clustering at +5 to +25 \u2014 a different object, not a marginal outlier. The injection work already had to be redone for having used this frame.",
   "robustness": "the rejection survives a 2x inflation of the frame-based SEs (chi2 74.6 -> 18.7, still > 9.49) but not 3x (-> 8.3). With n=4 the SE estimate itself carries only 3 dof."
  },
  "THE_LEVER_LIMITS_WHAT_f_CAN_EVER_BE": "the predicted trail vector varies only 5.1% in magnitude and 1.51 deg in axis across rho-equal bins, so f is nearly collinear with the constant K (design condition 131). This design can KILL the fix route and can never quote a trail scale.",
  "NOT_ATTEMPTED": "the PSFEx 2-D polynomial cross-check. It is a DIFFERENT ellipticity estimator (Moffat; psfex_compare.json already records a 0.038-vs-0.07 gap) and would need its own error model \u2014 and an unvalidated error model is precisely what this unit just showed to be worse than none."
 },
 "NAMED_ALTERNATIVE_TO_THE_VERDICT_demosaic": {
  "why_it_is_here": "raised by the PM mid-flight, verified by me IN THE SCRIPTS before recording: it bears directly on this fit's verdict.",
  "the_confound": "Siril's demosaic is a content-dependent nonlinear interpolation, and star shape varies across the field, so its contribution need NOT be common-mode across rho bins. An unmodelled rho-dependent demosaic term produces the SAME non-constancy this fit measures.",
  "status": "'there is no field-constant optical component' remains the LEADING reading of the failed constancy fit. It is NOT the only one. Not tested here, and it does not soften the verdict.",
  "the_processing-history_asymmetry_this_sits_on": {
   "verified_in_the_scripts": "inject_work/m2.ssf is `load injected2` -> `findstar` with NO convert, so the PLANTED stars never passed a demosaic; memraw_work/m.ssf runs `convert r -debayer`, so the REAL stars did; psf_calib.py's measure_all loads the fixture directly, so it is mono throughout.",
   "consequence": "the recorded contrast 'planted 0.99x against real 0.43x in the SAME frame, profile the only remaining difference' is FALSE as stated \u2014 the processing histories differ too."
  },
  "AND_IT_IS_MACHINE_STATE_NO_SCRIPT_CAN_PIN": {
   "config_DOES_record_it": "the [debayer] section carries `interpolation=8` (plus use_bayer_header=true, pattern=0). So the algorithm is not unrecorded \u2014 correcting the report that there is 'no algorithm key at all'.",
   "which_algorithm_8_is": "NOT established here. Siril's documented default is RCD; the enum mapping was not verified and is not asserted.",
   "but_it_is_unpinnable_from_a_script": "no `setdebayer` command exists (probed) and no command-like debayer string is present in the installed 1.4.4 binary, so an .ssf cannot pin it the way it pins setext/setcompress. Every measurement in this corpus therefore inherited whatever the machine-local config held, and no tracked script records which.",
   "class": "the same persisted-preference hazard as the FITS extension and setcompress, one step worse because the pinning mechanism does not exist."
  }
 }
}